# p10 negation: "this encounter has no glucose measurement"
#
# LinkML option: none.
#
# Two OWL forms, both about encounter1 in base.ttl:
#   1. Class membership in a complement, the OWL analogue of Wikidata's "no value":
#      encounter1 is a member of not (has part some 'glucose assay').
#   2. A NegativeObjectPropertyAssertion: encounter1 does not have ex:glucoseAssay1 as a part.
#      This is much weaker: it denies one named individual and says nothing about others.
#
# The prompt also mentioned NegativeDataPropertyAssertion. It does not fit this sentence: it
# denies one literal (e.g. "valueSpec1 does not have numeric value 95"), which presupposes a
# value specification and says nothing about the measurement being absent.
#
# A consumer with a reasoner can infer that any assertion of a glucose assay (or of any subclass,
# such as OBI:2100072) as part of encounter1 contradicts the record: see
# p10_negation_contradiction.ttl. A SPARQL consumer has to read the restriction structure;
# plain triple patterns see neither form as "no value".

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/encounter/> .
@prefix BFO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .

# Form 1
ex:encounter1 a
    [ a owl:Class ;
      owl:complementOf
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty BFO:0000051 ;
          owl:someValuesFrom OBI:2100020 ] ] .

# Form 2
ex:glucoseAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual .

[] a owl:NegativePropertyAssertion ;
    owl:sourceIndividual ex:encounter1 ;
    owl:assertionProperty BFO:0000051 ;
    owl:targetIndividual ex:glucoseAssay1 .
